    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52644" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλῐεπ-έομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>say in fine phrases</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὡς . . εἰκότως ἄρχομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.83
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ δοῦλος καλλιεποῖτο</span>
			<i>use fine language</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1404b16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥημάτων ὧν οἱ δεξιοὶ περὶ τὰς δίκας
					-εποῦνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Hipparch.</u>
					225c
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι κεκαλλιεπημένοι ῥήμασί τε καὶ
					ὀνόμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					17b
				</span></i>
			:—later in 
				Act.
			, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλιεπέω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				20p.285D.
			</span></i></div>
